Subject: [PATCH] wayland: detach the tablet's surface when freeing its cursor

The pointer and tablet cursor surfaces have independent lifetimes. The pointer
surface may be NULL when a tablet still references a replaced custom cursor.
Do not detach an unrelated pointer surface or dereference a NULL Wayland proxy.

--- a/src/video/wayland/SDL_waylandmouse.c
+++ b/src/video/wayland/SDL_waylandmouse.c
@@ -915,7 +915,7 @@ static void Wayland_FreeCursorData(SDL_CursorData *d)
 
                 // Custom cursor buffers are about to be destroyed, so ensure they are detached.
                 if (!d->is_system_cursor && tool->cursor_state.surface) {
-                    wl_surface_attach(seat->pointer.cursor_state.surface, NULL, 0, 0);
+                    wl_surface_attach(tool->cursor_state.surface, NULL, 0, 0);
                 }
 
                 tool->cursor_state.current_cursor = NULL;
